> Makes about 300 g. Quantities below are for the **base** ganache. See sections for butter and flavored variants.

Chop @dark chocolate{200%g} finely with a #knife{} (or grate coarsely on a #box grater{}).

In a #saucepan{}, bring @heavy cream{10%cl} to a boil over medium heat, then remove from the heat immediately. Pour the chocolate into the cream and stir off the heat until smooth and glossy.

Pour into a #bowl{}. Use at once, or let cool and set in the refrigerator.

== Ganache au beurre ==

Same method as the base, but use 11 cl cream (instead of 10 cl) and add @soft butter{40%g} to the hot cream at the same time as the chopped chocolate. Chocolate may be dark, milk, white, or mixed.

== Ganaches aromatisées ==

Same method as the base with 11 cl cream. First infuse the cream over low heat for about ~{5%minutes} with aromatics of your choice (coffee, spices, herbs, tea, etc.), then strain if needed and proceed with the chocolate.
